# FPS-MAC: the Mac frame rate, measured in a RELEASE editor and fixed at the root (owner 10-29: "что по фпс? Почему так
# мало?"). Each pass: Release profile -> the most expensive CPU zone -> the algorithm fixed -> the same profile again.
# The profile half runs headless, outside the scenario runner (no .scn keyword starts a profile capture; the runner
# plays the Debug editor). The SAME command runs on the base build and on the fixed build (build/Bin/Release/Editor):
#   Editor --project Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/FIELD_Barn.desce
#          --camera 0,170,2500 --look <dir of 1_eye> --shot <dir>/eye.png --shot-frames 300 --gpu-profile   (1_eye)
#          --camera 0,600,2500 --look <dir of 2_high> ...                                                   (2_high)
#   and Water_Ocean (../BistroFoliageProj/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/Water_Ocean.desce).
# [perf] PASS when, read from the two editor.log "[Profiler]" dumps of each view:
#   - fps (1000 / CPU frame ms) is higher after the fix on 1_eye and 2_high, and not lower on Water_Ocean;
#   - the ten most expensive CPU zones are listed before/after, GPU from the passes' own rows (not frame deltas);
#   - the after-frame of each view pixel-diffs < 0.5 % against the before-frame (scripts/Dev/frames_compare.py).
# The interactive half below shows the same two views in the editor, which must look as they did before the fix.
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/FIELD_Barn.desce
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,170,2500
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.15,-0.03,-1
Тогда-вид 1_eye FIELD_Barn at 1.7 m: the field, the barn and the sky look as before the fix (no missing shadows, no stale reflections)
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,600,2500
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.15,-0.12,-1
Тогда-вид 2_high FIELD_Barn at 6 m: the same field from above, shadows of the barn and trees present as before the fix
